- op: discuss  # 4f7e
  at: '2026-08-29T00:25:42Z'  # 4f7e
  by: agent  # 4f7e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4f7e
  clock: 3  # 4f7e
  nonce: 4f7e  # 4f7e
  message: "DONE in PR #618 (merged, dev at d2e4ef2203). All three deliverables shipped:\nthe directories, the subcommand, and seeded_from:.\n\nRE-RUN ON THE MERGED TREE, behaviourally, not by reading the diff:\n  hypergumbo init-catalogs  -> created 7 directories + README, seeded the 7\n                               community overlays into io_primitives.d/\n  dropped a user row in     -> io-boundaries reported 1 net_send chain for it\n  io_primitives.d/             on a throwaway repo\nSo the home exists AND is read, which are two different claims and the second\none is the one that was missing.\n\nDECISIONS I MADE, both reversible and recorded because ADR-0047 is silent:\n  * The subcommand is named `init-catalogs`, following the existing verb-first\n    build-grammars / install-embeddings shape. The ADR specifies \"an explicit\n    subcommand\" and never names one.\n  * All six registry-declared channel directories are created, not just the one\n    that is wired, so the layout is stable -- and the README written into the\n    home says PER FAMILY which are read today, rather than leaving a user to\n    discover an ignored overlay.\n\nSCOPE BEYOND THE ITEM, and why it was not optional. Nothing read\n$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hypergumbo/io_primitives.d/ -- the ADR-0045 `io_primitives`\nsetting is a list of paths a user NAMES, not a scan. Measured before the fix: a\nrow dropped there changed no boundary. Meanwhile the ruling-6 disclosure has\nbeen printing \"Override them in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hypergumbo/io_primitives.d/\"\non every run that loads a community overlay. Seeding files into an unread\ndirectory would have converted one false instruction into a much larger one, so\nthe scan is wired here, at the BOTTOM of the precedence chain (a path NAMED in\nconfig.toml beats a file dropped in a directory). It leans on INV-lufib for\nlanguage mismatch rather than inventing a second filter.\n\nTHREE DEFECTS THE TESTS FOUND, none by review:\n  1. The seeded files were being CORRUPTED. `!r` plus a trailing\n     .replace(\"'\", '\"') to get YAML double quotes -- and implicit string\n     concatenation binds BEFORE the method call, so the replace ran over the\n     whole file and turned every apostrophe in the source comments into a\n     quote. It would have written mangled prose into users' config homes. The\n     comment-preservation test caught it.\n  2. The did-you-mean guard's subcommand list was a hand-written literal.\n     `init-catalogs` parsed fine and was then rejected as \"not a valid\n     subcommand\" suggesting `catalog`. Now derived from the parser; the literal\n     held exactly the derived set (checked before the swap), so no behaviour\n     changed.\n  3. Which made an EXISTING gate fire: test_main_injection_subcommands_match_parser\n     parsed that literal out of main()'s source. Re-aimed rather than deleted --\n     it now asserts the DERIVATION is still in place, because reintroducing a\n     literal restores the hazard silently.\n\nNOT DONE HERE, stated so it is not assumed: repo_catalogue_home() NAMES\n<repo>/.hypergumbo/ and nothing loads it -- ruling 9 keeps that tier opt-in and\nforbids hypergumbo from writing into an analysed repo, and wiring the opt-in is\nWI-putat's. The other five channel directories are created but not consulted;\nwiring those loaders is WI-sofov's, and I verified the gap rather than assuming\nit (frameworks.d / function_summaries.d / dataflow_patterns.d / taint_sources.d\n/ taint_sanitizers.d have zero consumer references outside the registry).\n\nFull suite 24,639 passed / 0 failed. catalogue_home.py 100%, every new CLI line\ncovered."  # 4f7e
